 transfer agent, custodian, distributor, legal counsel, auditor, and pricing vendors. One provider can often cover several of these. The adviser may also house the CCO and valuation designee.\n\n**Market infrastructure:** Authorized participants, liquidity providers/market makers, exchange listing, DTC/NSCC clearing, and creation/redemption processing.\n\n**Strategy-specific only:**\n- Index provider and licensing (index-tracking funds)\n- Securities lending agent (if lending)\n- Liquidity risk program under Rule 22e-4 (if applicable)\n- Derivatives risk program under Rule 18f-4, ISDA agreements, and FCM (if using derivatives or futures)\n- Sub-adviser (multi-manager structures)\n- Offshore subsidiary (commodity or tax structures)","ttft_ms":5098,"type":"result","duration_ms":6444,"uuid":"89a4582e-869b-40b5-9f35-af539683908c","ttft_stream_ms":421,"time_to_request_ms":71,"first_content_frame_ms":422,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
